As many SAG -AFTRA members struggle to qualify for health insurance, the union is taking the issue to the U.S. government.

On Friday, Screen Actors Guild President Sean Astin announced the President's Healthcare Task Force to address the "broken healthcare system" while several actors have faced losing their insurance under the union's minimum eligibility requirements.

"This is a critical moment, where both our members and the public at large can no longer wait for relief from a broken healthcare system," he said in a statement . "Our SAG-AFTRA Health Plan is healthy and strong, but a substantial majority of our members do not qualify. For our members who don't qualify, there is very little that can be done to provide coverage." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Astin added, "SAG-AFTRA has supported efforts to expand healthcare for all through the AFL-CIO. This task force seeks a new level of participation in the national movement to expand care for everyone. We will actively engage with policymakers, gather allies and provide a structured way for our members to participate formally in the process. The President's Healthcare Task Force will be an instrument of support in the movement for universal healthcare." Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The SAG-AFTRA National Board voted unanimously on Friday to form the Task Force, which seeks to mobilize SAG-AFTRA's collective strength and public influence to fight for universal access to affordable, comprehensive and reliable health care.

SAG's new initiative comes amid financial scrutiny for the union following National Executive Director Duncan Crabtree-Ireland's recent contract renewal , after his salary surpassed $1M in 2023.

Sorry, &#x201C; Succession &#x201D; fans &#x2014; Kieran Culkin is shutting down any possibility of a spinoff once and for all.

The actor, currently starring in &#x201C;The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping&#x201D; as a young Caesar Flickerman, joined the &#x201C;Heart Breakfast&#x201D; radio show on Friday to discuss the new film, though hosts Amanda Holden and Jamie Theakston also snuck in a few questions regarding the hit HBO show&#x2019;s potential future. Related Stories Qatar Film Chief Hassan Al Thawadi Says World Cup Success Paved Way for Hollywood Push, Signals Next Steps on Neon Deal ‘Once Upon a Time in Harlem’ Duo Praise Neon’s Strategy to Reach Young Audiences

&#x201C;I know we&#x2019;re not here to talk about this, but I&#x2019;m still grieving the end of &#x2018;Succession,&#x2019;&#x201D; said Holden, to which Culkin responded: &#x201C;Oh, you are? Get over it. It&#x2019;s been three years!&#x201D; When asked about a potential for a spinoff, Culkin answered, &#x201C;Of course not. I think that would be a terrible idea&#x2026; I mean, what are you hoping for? 'Cousin Greg: The Sitcom?'… Yeah, that would be a terrible idea.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

And though the &#x201C;A Real Pain&#x201D; actor is steadfast about not retreading the show's familiar territory, he noted that he misses playing Roman Roy and the &#x201C;whole thing.&#x201D;

Culkin continued: &#x201C;It was fun. It was one of those where Jesse Armstrong, the showrunner, spent the entire last season trying to figure out if there was a way to do one more. I never wanted to know what was going to happen in the season and on the fourth one I did ask and when he pitched me the end of the season and I went &#x2018;well, that kind of sounds like it&#x2019;s the end of the show.&#x2019; But when he pitched me three different ideas of what season 5 could be, they all sounded good&#x2026; But it ended perfectly. The way it was supposed to.

Elsewhere in the interview, Culkin divulged that he&#x2019;ll be reuniting with &#x201C;Succession&#x201D; creator Jesse Armstrong on a new film. Culkin starred alongside Brian Cox, Sarah Snook, Jeremy Strong, Nicholas Braun, Matthew Macfadyen, Alan Ruck and more in the acclaimed drama, which ran for four seasons. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

