As Nickerson explained it was an "incredible gift" to know they were ending after Season 4 , Lyle noted that they were "reinvigorated" to get to return to civilization, which had always been their plan for the final season.

"We had been looking forward to that for so long now. It was part of the original pitch, and to finally get there&#x2014;everything, when you're pitching a show, it all feels like a pipe dream," said Lyle. "You don't think you're actually going to be able to do any of this, especially something that you know is only gonna be if you get a first season, a second season, a third season. So, to actually reach that point and get to dive in, it reinvigorated everybody." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In Yellowjackets , a 1996 New Jersey soccer team's plane crashes in the Canadian wilderness, where they struggle to survive while they're stranded for 19 months as a dark supernatural force seemingly lurks in the woods. Meanwhile, their adult counterparts cope with the memories of what went down in the wilderness.

With new episodes available to stream Fridays on Paramount+ with Premium Plan, the fourth and final season sees the Yellowjackets rescued and returned home, where they must adjust to civilization and take their secrets to the grave.

Russell Brand is selling merchandise calling for his freedom while he's behind bars after being sentenced to 10 years and six months in prison after being found guilty of rape and sexual assault.

The actor has three items featuring "Free Russell" available for purchase on the website for Reborn, his wellness business. Every item is available for $34.99; a shirt with the words "Free Russell Brand "; a hat with the same text; and another shirt that reads "Free Russell" with an image of himself.

Upon visiting the Reborn website, images of the merch are displayed on its homepage with text that reads, "Stand with Russell against injustice" and "silenced for speaking out." After clicking on the "Free Russell" section of the site, the items are labeled as "fundraiser apparel," with a descriptor that additionally reads, "Silenced for speaking out against injustuce and corruption." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Google Says It's Investigating Russell Brand YouTube Video Where He Said He's "Not Guilty" in Message From Prison News Over 400 U.K. Industry Figures Demand End to "Culture of Open Secrets" After Russell Brand Trial

It is unclear how long the items have been available for purchase on Reborn, however the earliest reviews on the varying products date to Nov. 16 (he was sentenced Nov. 9). Brand recently received backlash for sharing a message from prison , delivered by his wife, Laura Brand, on his YouTube channel where he claimed he was innocent.

&#x201C;So Russell has asked me to read something to you today,&#x201D; the actor&#x2019;s wife said at the start of the video, before looking to a notebook to read her husband&#x2019;s message. &#x201C;Beloved brothers and sisters in Christ, God bless you for your support. As you know, I am not guilty for the offenses I have been jailed for, so something strange is happening.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Brand was sentenced to 10 years and six months in prison after being found guilty of rape and sexual assault. The trial lasted four weeks at Southwark Crown Court, with the jury finding him guilty on one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault (he was found not guilty on two other rape charges and not guilty of attempted indecent assault).

After the YouTube video was shared, Google, the parent company of YouTube, told BBC News it was &#x201C;aware of the new content and our teams are investigating,&#x201D; adding, &#x201C;We suspended Russell Brand&#x2019;s channel from the YouTube Partner Program in September 2023. The channel has not been able to monetise on YouTube since then.&#x201D;

BBC News also reported that Google declined a request from the Ministry of Justice to remove the video, saying none of its rules had been broken.

His message, delivered by his wife in the YouTube video, drew criticism, with Britain&#x2019;s Justice Secretary Alex Norris calling the broadcast of a statement from Brand while he is behind bars &#x201C;completely unacceptable.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Prisoners are rightly banned from making statements that cause distress to victims,&#x201D; Norris wrote on X. &#x201C;This is being urgently investigated, and I expect action to be taken if he is found to have broken the rules.&#x201D;

Mahershala Ali got candid about the impact &#x2014; or lack thereof &#x2014; his two Oscar wins have had on his career in Hollywood while appearing on a recent episode of Carmelo Anthony and Kazeem &#x201C;Kaz&#x201D; Famuyide&#x2019;s &#x201C;7PM in Brooklyn&#x201D; podcast.

The actor, who took home trophies for best supporting actor for both 2018&#x2019;s &#x201C; Greenbook &#x201D; and 2016&#x2019;s &#x201C; Moonlight ,&#x201D; asked the hosts about the meaning of an Oscar, and if it really validates whether someone is &#x201C;a good actor&#x201D; or not. &#x201C;There&#x2019;s more good actors than there is good material,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not even that all these people are competing for these same spots. It&#x2019;s just that out of all the material made, there&#x2019;s only a handful of them that check certain boxes.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Stage Adaptation of Amanda Seyfried, Sydney Sweeney-Starrer 'The Housemaid' Sets London Premiere Lionsgate Quarterly Revenue Pops 41% on Strength of 'Michael,' TV Series Sales as Studio Narrows Net Loss

He continued: &#x201C;The vast majority of projects that get greenlit, there are not roles for me in those. You gotta think that way, you know what I mean? So, it doesn&#x2019;t matter if I got 17 Oscars. If someone is not writing something for you or greenlighting something with you in mind, you&#x2019;re like everybody else waiting and looking and searching.&#x201D;

While the star noted that actors could produce their own projects, the timeline is usually as least a &#x201C;three to five year&#x201D; journey. When asked by Famuyide if an Oscar win validates Black actors, Ali responded: &#x201C;It&#x2019;s kind of just talk. It doesn&#x2019;t translate to anything real. You don&#x2019;t want to find yourself in a situation where, oh, that&#x2019;s &#x2018;the diversity project.&#x2019; You just want to do great material as a Black person. You&#x2019;re not thinking of yourself as this exotic other, per se. You just are living your life.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Most recently, Ali starred in Bassam Tariq&#x2019;s &#x201C; Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother ,&#x201D; which hit theaters on Sept. 25. Tariq was also the original director of Marvel&#x2019;s failed &#x201C;Blade&#x201D; movie , in which Ali was set to star in the title role, which he recently discussed in an interview with The New Arab.

&#x201C;It was funny and strange to start casting and building without a proper script,&#x201D; Tariq told interviewer Hanna Flint about his short-lived Marvel career. &#x201C;You&#x2019;re sitting there and explaining to actors what their role will be, and they just have to believe you. That&#x2019;s also very dangerous because if the text comes and it doesn&#x2019;t add up to what you were saying, your credibility gets completely shot. All I have is my integrity, and I&#x2019;ve been thinking about that a lot.&#x201D;

&#x201C;If you&#x2019;re the bearer of bad news to your actors, but you&#x2019;re not the one making any of these decisions &#x2014; and it&#x2019;s actually coming from a corporate entity &#x2014; that&#x2019;s not a great way to be a director,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;I know some people can take that and run with it, but I learned I was losing credibility with my actors, and it wasn&#x2019;t a healthy way to operate as a filmmaker. Life&#x2019;s too short to make shit films, so that was my big lesson: I have to have full control over my script. If we disagree, it&#x2019;s between them and me. It&#x2019;s quite sad because we had such high hopes for what we wanted to build.&#x201D;

Speaking of the film&#x2019;s inability to get made, Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige had previously said he felt &#x201C;like a gigantic loser and failure,&#x201D; a statement that Ali agreed with in a GQ interview in the months following. &#x201C;To this day, I don&#x2019;t know why it didn&#x2019;t happen. I just know that it was&#x2014;Kevin, he said it was the biggest failure of his career and I agree,&#x201D; said Ali.

